<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE -ROMATEX NINE-MO SHR FALLS INTO LOSS.</title>
<headline>TABLE -ROMATEX NINE-MO SHR FALLS INTO LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year/Half year ended</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		 32 loss    vs 14 profit</p>
<p>    - attrib		   64 loss    vs 17 profit</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs  4</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    16.1 loss  vs  4.3 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    24.7 loss  vs  0.1 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			   8.6	 vs  4.2</p>
<p>    Turnover		  372.0	 vs 505.3</p>
<p>    Abnormal items(*)	12.6	 vs   0.0</p>
<p>Full name: Romatex Ltd</p>
<p>(*)Abnormal items represent a combination of rationalisation costs and a provision in respect of a lease commitment following the closure of the Johannesburg distribution centre for the carpets division.</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said focused initiatives were under way to stem its losses and stabilise the situation. In addition, the group needed an upgrading of technology and management skills in key areas.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
